CONTENT
Playbook ID: RD-004. Title: "RD-004: A UI Review Bundles the Frontend Surface".
What it verifies: a review request about a UI component returns the review mode first and the frontend surface second, so the reviewer reads the frontend standards as evidence. The risk it guards: the review keyword alone outscored every frontend phrase, so a UI review loaded no frontend reference.
Realistic user request: a developer asks for a review of a component and names accessibility.
Exact prompt:
review my react component for accessibility issues
Preconditions: node is callable, and `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs --json` reports the sk-code hub as fresh.
Exact Command Sequence: 1. run: node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-code --prompt "review my react component for accessibility issues" > /tmp/skc-RD004-route.txt  2. run: grep -o '"workflowMode":"[a-z-]*"' /tmp/skc-RD004-route.txt
Expected signals: "selectionKind":"surfaceBundle", and the second command prints "workflowMode":"sk-code-review" on its first line and "workflowMode":"sk-code-frontend" on its second line.
PASS iff the route holds exactly those two targets in that order. FAIL iff sk-code-frontend is missing, or it is the only target, or it comes first.
Evidence: /tmp/skc-RD004-route.txt
Failure triage: 1. The router bundles two modes only when their scores tie, and each distinct matched phrase scores once. 2. If sk-code-frontend is missing, no frontend phrase matched, so add one review-oriented phrase to the code-frontend-review class in hub-router.json. 3. If sk-code-frontend is the only target, two frontend phrases matched the prompt and outscored the review mode, so remove the broader of the two. 4. Never edit the prompt to make it pass.

VERIFY (run from the repository root):
grep -c '^## [1-5]\. ' .skilled/skills/sk-code/manual-testing-playbook/routing-disambiguation/frontend-review-bundle.md
